    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="d394-2" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v10-12mSupp/d394-2"/>

                <head>395. Memorandum of telephone conversation between Ball and McGeorge Bundy,
                    October 25<anchor n="1" xml:id="d395-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1962-10-25T01:00:00">October 25, 1962, 1
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d395-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d395-1"/>
                <p>Bundy said that the President wants to go along with Ball’s version. He said that since we can’t get any agreement on
                    the longer version, they will go along with the short version. Bunday said that
                    they will have to get across to Adlai—</p>
                <p>Ball said he was talking with Cleveland and that he doesn’t think we can
                    soften it any. Ball said that we are
                    going to have to think about getting McCloy down—Bundy agreed that Ball should ask McCloy
                    to come down.</p>
                <p>Bundy said that the President just came into the room and he said that he thought
                    the first clause of paragraph 3 . . . in order to give time might mean we
                    willing to give. Can’t we leave that out?</p>
                <p>Bundy and Ball agreed that the 3rd and
                    4th paragraphs could be put together.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
